# TypeScript Engineering Rules

These rules specialize the shared engineering constitution for Auto-QA.

## Test-first delivery
- Use red/green TDD through only the public seams in
  `docs/testing-strategy.md`.
- Prefer real temporary SQLite stores and deterministic system-boundary
  adapters over mocks of Auto-QA modules.
- Use Vitest for all ordinary and integration test execution.
- Use fast-check for state-machine sequences, round trips, idempotence, and
  other genuine invariants.
- Use StrykerJS with its Vitest runner for the selected pure modules assigned to
  the deep gate. Keep mutation runs separate from normal tests.
- Use `jscpd` for report-only duplication detection; do not mechanically merge
  merely similar code.

## Package management
- Add packages with `fnm exec --using 22 pnpm add` and development packages
  with `fnm exec --using 22 pnpm add --save-dev`.
- Run package scripts with `fnm exec --using 22 pnpm <script>`.
- Do not replace pnpm with npm, Bun, or Yarn.

## Effect and boundaries
- Model services, scoped resources, failures, clocks, and process ownership
  with Effect.
- Keep the Workflow Engine independent of argv, stdout, Commander, Playwright,
  and SQLite representation details.
- Put Git, SQLite, Playwright, filesystem, process, time, and randomness behind
  narrow domain-oriented boundaries.
- Do not abstract Playwright's author-facing Scenario Script API; abstract the
  execution runtime owned by Auto-QA.

## Acceptance pipeline
- Keep approved Gherkin under `features/`.
- Keep project-specific TypeScript generators, handlers, and runners under
  `acceptance/`.
- Keep parser IR and generated entrypoints under ignored `build/acceptance/`
  paths.
- Use the APS-supplied `gherkin-parser`; do not reimplement it.
- Prefer a stable in-process public seam for early acceptance slices, adding the
  packaged CLI and real browser only when the behavior requires those seams.
